1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,010
Why does your controller shake when you

2
00:00:02,010 --> 00:00:02,710
crash?

3
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:05,460
Every hit, every crash, you feel it in

4
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:07,560
your hands... and it all comes from one

5
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,810
lopsided weight.

6
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:11,200
Inside each handle is a tiny motor.

7
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,460
On its shaft sits a weight that's heavier

8
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,410
on one side.

9
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:17,170
When it spins, that uneven weight yanks

10
00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:19,250
the controller back and forth, dozens of

11
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:20,020
times a second.

12
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:22,380
On many controllers, the left weight is

13
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:23,840
heavy, for deep rumbles.

14
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,530
The right one is light, for quick buzzes.

15
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:29,230
Newer controllers add magnet coils for

16
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:31,650
tiny taps... but that crash you just felt?

17
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:32,790
A spinning weight.
